  "articleBody": "When you're trying to fix a small drywall issue, it's surprisingly easy to make a few common missteps that can lead to bigger problems or a less-than-perfect finish. One of the biggest no-nos is patching over damp or wet material. If there's any moisture present, you absolutely have to find and fix the leak first and dry out the area completely. Skipping this step is just asking for mold and repeat damage. Another frequent mistake is not addressing the underlying cause of the damage. If a leak caused the problem, and you just patch the drywall, you'll be dealing with the same issue again soon. It's like putting a band-aid on a broken leg! You also want to avoid leaving hidden damage behind the wall. Sometimes, what looks like a small surface crack can be a sign of a larger issue with the framing or insulation. And finally, poor finishing that leaves the patch visible after painting is a huge giveaway that the repair wasn't done correctly. You want that repair to blend in seamlessly. To steer clear of these mistakes, choose a professional who can properly assess the damage, handle any moisture concerns, and ensure a flawless finish. HH Remodeling LLC, serving areas like Lakewood and Golden, is here to help you avoid these headaches.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
